  "title": "Resolve place name"
 },
 "description": "Turn a place name ('outside Halifax', 'Strait of Hormuz', 'Bergen,\n    Norway') into water coordinates. Maritime gazetteer first (ports resolve\n    to their approaches, straits/seas to a representative point), then\n    OpenStreetMap. Points on land or shallower than min_depth_m are walked\n    seaward along the gazetteer bearing (or the nearest direction) until deep\n    enough; the original point and the snap are reported. offshore_km pushes\n    the point further out along seaward_bearing_deg. All location tools also\n    accept `place` directly, so a separate call is only needed to inspect.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "min_depth_m": {
    "default": 10.0,
    "title": "Min Depth M",
    "type": "number"
   },
   "offshore_km": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "type": "number"
     },
     {
      "type": "null"
     }
    ],
    "default": null,
    "title": "Offshore Km"
   },
   "place": {
    "title": "Place",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "seaward_bearing_deg": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
